data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dispatch_dev_1.md\", \"content\": \"Task: implement \\\"greet, tested\\\" in the subject repository.\\n\\nDeliver both of the following in your repo, on your own branch:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` containing a function `greet(name)` that returns the exact\\n   string `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (e.g. `greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` with unittest tests covering:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\nThen run this exact command yourself and confirm it exits 0:\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\nBefore replying:\\n- Make sure the command above actually passes (paste its output in your reply).\\n- Commit your work to your own branch.\\n- In your reply, state the exit code of the test run and the branch/commit you\\n  committed to.\\n\\nImplement exactly this — no extra scope, no unrelated changes.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

